+# Privacy by Design — The Daily Grind website
+
+How privacy is built into this site. Run `npm run audit:privacy` before every
+deploy; it enforces most of the rules below automatically.
+
+## 1. Principles applied
+
+| Principle | Implementation |
+|---|---|
+| Proactive, not reactive | `scripts/audit-privacy.mjs` blocks unaudited third parties, inline code and missing headers before release. |
+| Privacy as the default | All non-essential categories are off. Without consent nothing optional runs, and the consent prompt is shown only if a non-essential vendor is actually registered. |
+| Embedded into design | Strict CSP (`default-src 'none'`, self-only), `Referrer-Policy: same-origin`, restrictive `Permissions-Policy`, and no inline script or style. |
+| Full functionality | Reject and accept buttons have equal weight; the site works fully with everything rejected. |
+| End-to-end security | HSTS (with preload), `upgrade-insecure-requests`, logout via POST, and `Clear-Site-Data` on logout. |
+| Visibility & transparency | "Privacy Choices" in the footer shows the current state, and `/.well-known/gpc.json` declares GPC support. |
+| Respect for the user | Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track signals are honoured automatically. |
+
+## 2. Data inventory (client side)
+
+| Data | Where | Purpose | Retention |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `dg_privacy_consent`: `{v, date (YYYY-MM-DD), analytics, marketing}` | `localStorage` | Remember the privacy choice | Auto-deleted after 12 months or on version change |
+| Session cookie (set by the backend) | Cookie | Sign-in | Session; removed on logout |
+
+Nothing else is stored. The page holds no identifiers, fingerprinting, or
+analytics. Tracking query parameters (`utm_*`, `gclid`, `fbclid`, `msclkid`, …)
+are removed from the address bar on load, so they don't end up in bookmarks,
+shared links or the same-origin referrer. On logout, `sessionStorage` and all
+`dg_*` `localStorage` keys except the consent choice are cleared client side.
+The server also sends `Clear-Site-Data`.
+
+## 3. Third-party audit
+
+The register is `privacy/third-parties.json`. Current state (audited
+2026-11-11): **no third-party origins are contacted.**
+
+| Removed | Why | Replacement |
+|---|---|---|
+| `images.unsplash.com` (hero image hotlink) | Leaked every visitor's IP, user agent and referrer on page load. | Self-hosted at `assets/img/hero-coffee.jpg` (Unsplash License, no EXIF metadata). |
+
+To add a vendor (all steps are required, and the audit fails otherwise):
+1. Complete a DPIA / vendor review: purpose, data shared, DPA, retention, and data location.
+2. Add the vendor to `privacy/third-parties.json` → `allowed`.
+3. If it is non-essential, register it in `THIRD_PARTIES` in `assets/js/privacy.js`. It will then load only after consent, with `referrerpolicy=no-referrer` and SRI where possible.
+4. Extend the CSP with the narrowest possible source in **both** `index.html` and `_headers`.
+
+## 4. Security headers
+
+The headers are defined in `_headers` (Netlify / Cloudflare Pages format). The
+local `statikk` dev server does not read that file. The CSP and referrer policy
+are therefore also set via `<meta>` in the HTML, so they apply everywhere.
+`frame-ancestors`, HSTS, `Permissions-Policy` and the other headers below only
+take effect when they are sent as real HTTP headers.
+
+nginx equivalent:
+
+```nginx
+add_header Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests" always;
+add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload" always;
+add_header Referrer-Policy "same-origin" always;
+add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff" always;
+add_header X-Frame-Options "DENY" always;
+add_header Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy "same-origin" always;
+add_header Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy "same-origin" always;
+add_header Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy "require-corp" always;
+add_header Permissions-Policy "camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(self), browsing-topics=(), interest-cohort=(), usb=(), serial=(), hid=()" always;
+location = /logout { add_header Clear-Site-Data '"cache", "cookies", "storage"' always; }
+location ~ ^/(account|rewards|order-online) { add_header Cache-Control "no-store" always; }
+```
+
+## 5. Backend requirements (outside this repo)
+
+- Session cookies: `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax` (or `Strict`), with a `__Host-` prefix and no `Domain` attribute.
+- `POST /logout`: verify the `Origin` header or a CSRF token, invalidate the session server side, and respond with `Clear-Site-Data`.
+- Logs: truncate IP addresses or drop them after a short retention window, and never log query strings that contain personal data.
+- Honour the `Sec-GPC: 1` request header server side as an opt-out of sale or sharing.
